(Q4 - Brute-Force Closest Pair of Points \(6 Marks\)) Tj
50 671.0 Td
(==================================================) Tj
50 658.0 Td
(Problem: Drone monitoring system finds the two drones closest to each other.) Tj
50 645.0 Td
() Tj
50 632.0 Td
() Tj
50 619.0 Td
(ALGORITHM: BruteForceClosestPair\(P[0..n-1]\)) Tj
50 606.0 Td
(--------------------------------------------) Tj
50 593.0 Td
(// Find the pair of points with minimum Euclidean distance) Tj
50 580.0 Td
(// Input : Array P of n points, each P[i] = \(x_i, y_i\)) Tj
50 567.0 Td
(// Output: Indices of closest pair, minimum distance, distance_calculations count) Tj
50 554.0 Td
() Tj
50 541.0 Td
(  min_dist  <- INFINITY) Tj
50 528.0 Td
(  pair      <- \(-1, -1\)) Tj
50 515.0 Td
(  dist_calcs <- 0) Tj
50 502.0 Td
() Tj
50 489.0 Td
(  FOR i <- 0 TO n-2 DO) Tj
50 476.0 Td
(      FOR j <- i+1 TO n-1 DO) Tj
50 463.0 Td
(          dist_calcs <- dist_calcs + 1) Tj
50 450.0 Td
(          d <- SQRT\(\(P[i].x - P[j].x\)^2 + \(P[i].y - P[j].y\)^2\)) Tj
50 437.0 Td
(          IF d < min_dist THEN) Tj
50 424.0 Td
(              min_dist <- d) Tj
50 411.0 Td
(              pair     <- \(i, j\)) Tj
50 398.0 Td
(          END IF) Tj
50 385.0 Td
(      END FOR) Tj
50 372.0 Td
(  END FOR) Tj
50 359.0 Td
(  RETURN pair, min_dist, dist_calcs) Tj
50 346.0 Td
() Tj
50 333.0 Td
(Step-by-Step Logic:) Tj
50 320.0 Td
(  1. Initialise minimum distance to infinity.) Tj
50 307.0 Td
(  2. Consider every distinct pair \(i, j\) where i < j.) Tj
50 294.0 Td
(  3. For each pair, compute Euclidean distance d\(P_i, P_j\).) Tj
50 281.0 Td
(  4. If this distance is smaller than current minimum, update.) Tj
50 268.0 Td
(  5. After all pairs examined, return the closest pair.) Tj
50 255.0 Td
(  6. Total pairs considered = n\(n-1\)/2.) Tj
50 242.0 Td
() Tj
50 229.0 Td
() Tj
50 216.0 Td
(CANDIDATE PAIR REPRESENTATION) Tj
50 203.0 Td
(===============================) Tj
50 190.0 Td
(  - Each candidate is an unordered pair {i, j} with i < j.) Tj
50 177.0 Td
(  - Total candidates = C\(n,2\) = n\(n-1\)/2.) Tj
50 164.0 Td
(  - For n=10: 45 pairs | n=100: 4,950 | n=1000: 499,500) Tj
50 151.0 Td
() Tj
50 138.0 Td
() Tj
50 125.0 Td
(DISTANCE CALCULATION) Tj
50 112.0 Td
(=====================) Tj
50 99.0 Td
(  Euclidean distance:) Tj
50 86.0 Td
(    d\(P_i, P_j\) = sqrt\( \(x_i - x_j\)^2 + \(y_i - y_j\)^2 \)) Tj
50 73.0 Td
() Tj
